=== APPROACH ===
- The repository's WinUI app is code-first C# (no .xaml page files); every feature surface lives under
  apps/windows/TeslaSync.App/feature-views/<Name>/ as <Name>.Model.cs (+ parsers + registration + the i18n
  resolver), <Name>.Projection.cs (pure, Microsoft.UI-free projection, unit-tested headlessly),
  <Name>.Source.cs (generated-client feed, ADR-004), <Name>.ViewModel.cs (INotifyPropertyChanged + IDisposable
  observable state holder) and <Name>.cs (the Fluent view). The generated prompt's idealized
  "StateMachineDebuggerPage.xaml + StateMachineDebuggerPageViewModel.cs under TeslaSync/Features/System" is mapped
  onto these real conventions (same mapping as every shipped W7 page, e.g. DataRepairPage / CommandHistoryPage).
- Namespace: the page lives in TeslaSync.App.FeatureViews.Telemetry (matching the sibling TelemetrySignals pages
  LiveSignalMonitorPage / SignalDiffPage / SignalsWorkspacePage and the route's RouteGroup.TelemetrySignals; a
  ".System" leaf would shadow the global System namespace). RouteTable already maps
  Page("StateMachineDebugger","state-debugger",RouteGroup.TelemetrySignals,"State Debugger"); the surface registers
  itself with the W4 ShellPageFactory by that exact route name in Shell/ShellWindow.xaml.cs.
- Data sources bound to the generated C# client (ADR-004) through StateMachineDebuggerClientFeed in
  StateMachineDebuggerPage.Source.cs — the five operations verified present in
  apps/windows/Generated/Api/ApiEndpoints.cs:
    useSelectedVehicle vehicles -> GET /vehicles/                     (get_api_v1_vehicles)
    useVehicleStateMachine      -> GET /vehicles/{id}/state           (get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_state)
    useFSMStats                 -> GET /fsm/stats                     (get_api_v1_fsm_stats)
    useFSMTransitions           -> GET /fsm/transitions               (get_api_v1_fsm_transitions)
    useSignalSnapshot           -> GET /signals/{id}/snapshot         (get_api_v1_signals_vehicleID_snapshot)
  The endpoints declare no typed query params, so the client appends vehicle_id/fsm/hours/page/per_page/at as
  snake_case (BuildQuery allows free params when the descriptor declares none). The default
  EmptyStateMachineDebuggerFeed resolves the no-backend states (the shell uses the parameterless ctor); the
  view-model is exercised in tests with a FakeFeed driving the loading/empty/success matrix + the snapshot fetch.
- Composition: the page reproduces every web region by composing the FSM sub-surfaces already built for it —
  FSMHealthPanel (ns .Fsm), FSMSubFSMPanel, FSMTimelineChart, SnapshotInspector (ns .FeatureViews), StateTimeline +
  LiveControls (ns .StateMachine) and FSMStateDiagram (ns .FeatureViews). The pure projection builds each
  sub-surface's data model (FsmHealthPanelModel / FSMSubFSMPanelModel / FSMTimelineChartModel / StateTimelineModel /
  LiveControlsModel / SnapshotInspectorModel) so the view stays a thin renderer. FSMStateDiagram is a self-fetching
  surface; the page hosts it over the no-backend EmptyFsmStateDiagramSource (mirroring the empty-feed default).
- AI narrator (web AIStateMachineDebuggerNarrator, withAiFeature) is a SEPARATE parity unit and is intentionally
  out of scope here (it is not among the 11 manifest panels and renders null when the toggle is off) — the same
  treatment the shipped DataRepairPage applied to its AIDataRepairSuggestions panel.
- SI: the page carries no display-boundary unit conversion of its own — the FSM transition log is a
  state-machine trace (states / triggers / timestamps / counts), not a metric surface. The sub-surfaces that do
  show units (e.g. the snapshot inspector) format at the display boundary inside their own ports. Times are
  rendered with invariant clock/relative formatters in the pure projection.
- Strings: every visible literal resolves through ILocalizer with the exact web t() key + English fallback
  (StateMachineDebuggerStrings / FsmTypeCatalog / StateMachineDebuggerRegistration), the established windows
  convention; the page renders correct English via key-fallback whether or not Strings/*.resw carries the key.
- Predecessor (W1): the gitignored generated OpenAPI C# client was regenerated for this environment via
  `pwsh apps/tools/codegen/gen-clients.ps1` (10 C# files under apps/windows/Generated/Api/) and its referencing
  project apps/windows/Generated/Generated.csproj (a regenerated, gitignored build artifact) reconstituted so the
  data layer compiles.

